--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (cross-platform value parity, NOT a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data sources bound via the P1/S8 seam (no view HTTP): useVehicles + useVehicleState (state.software_version)
    + useVehicleConfigLatest (software_update_version / _download_pct / _install_pct / _expected_duration /
    _scheduled_start). `state` falsy -> empty "No software data"; present -> content.
  updateStatus useMemo reproduced VERBATIM (branch order preserved): !updateVersion (or "") -> up-to-date ;
    installPct in (0,100) -> installing ; downloadPct in (0,100) -> downloading ; installPct == 100 ->
    installed ; downloadPct == 100 -> ready ; else available. install-in-progress is checked BEFORE download;
    installed (==100) BEFORE ready (==100). (Pinned by executed assertions.)
  StatusBadgeSmall config reproduced: up-to-date=success "Up to date" ; available=info "Available" ;
    downloading=warning "Downloading" ; ready=info "Ready" ; installing=warning "Installing" ;
    installed=success "Installed". Variants mapped onto shared tokens via TSTone (success->statusSuccess,
    info->statusInfo, warning->statusWarning, neutral->textMuted); the chip carries a leading dot (web `dot`).
  FullView render gates reproduced: current-version row always (version || '—' ; badge right) ; update section
    iff (updateVersion && stage != up-to-date) ; download bar #22d3ee->Color.TS.statusInfo (cyan) ; install bar
    #a78bfa->Color.TS.chartSeriesPower (violet) ; "Ready to install" row (stage==ready) ; Est.-time row iff
    (isTall && expectedDuration>0) ; Scheduled row iff (isTall && scheduledStart) ; "Up to date" footer iff
    stage==up-to-date. ${pct}% rendered without a trailing .0 for whole numbers (JS `${47}` -> "47").
  isCompact = cols<=1 && rows<=1 (defensive parity branch, kept reachable for previews/tests; under the registry
    min 1x2 the grid never reaches it, exactly as the web source); isTall = rows>=2. MetricBar fill =
    min(max(value/100,0),1). The view renders the grid-supplied size; the registry envelope is honored by the
    tested registration.clamp(_:), so the surface "respects the same size constraints" without self-clamping
    away the compact branch.
  i18n: every web key present in the catalog (widget.softwareUpdate, widget.noSoftwareData, widget.currentVersion,
    widget.updateAvailable, widget.downloading, widget.installing, widget.readyToInstall, widget.estimatedTime,
    widget.minutes, widget.scheduledStart, widget.upToDate, widget.statusUpToDate/Available/Downloading/Ready/
    Installing/Installed); no English literal ships (all via SoftwareStatusStrings). Domain types are namespaced
    SoftwareStatus* (the sibling SoftwareUpdateHistoryWidget already owns SoftwareUpdate*/SoftwareUpdateStatus*/
    SoftwareUpdateStatusChip in this single module) to avoid duplicate-symbol collisions.

